    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG Dorrian are delighted to present to the market this beautifully upgraded and extended three-bedroom detached residence, occupying a truly stunning and tranquil setting amid rolling countryside and mature landscaped gardens. Lovingly improved by the current owners, the property offers a warm, character-filled home where carefully considered upgrades and extensions have created bright, comfortable and highly appealing living accommodation. The interiors are tastefully presented throughout, with generous reception space, large picture windows framing the surrounding landscape, and an inviting layout that perfectly complements the peaceful rural surroundings.\n\nOne of the standout features of this exceptional property is undoubtedly its magnificent gardens that span an impressive circa 1.18 acres in area. Carefully nurtured over time, the grounds have evolved into a private oasis for wildlife, with mature trees, colourful planting, natural shelter, lawned areas and established borders creating a rich and welcoming habitat for the owners beloved guinea fowl plus other native birds, bees, butterflies. The gardens provide a wonderful sense of seclusion and seasonal colour, offering a peaceful sanctuary for those who appreciate nature, privacy and outdoor living."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nSitting Room: - 5.6m x 4.3m\nwith two large windows looking out over the garden, wooden front door, ceramic tiled floor, cast iron affect frosted glass centre light, PSTN wall socket.\n\nSnug / Living Room: - 8.9m x 3.7m\nincorporating a formal dining space, carpet floor covering, oak stairs with enclosed treads and risers and oak stairs, two centre lights, arch in the kitchen, frosted glass centre door, thermostatic wall stat, built-in hotpress with factory-insulated cylinder tank, EPH three zone heating clock, coaxial TV point.\n\nKitchen / Diner: - 5.4m x 2.7m\nwith comprehensive range of solid wall and base units with chunky wooden worktops, built-in chest-level double oven with stainless steel surround, built-in induction hob with extractor canopy over, integrated fridge/freezer and slot-in washing machine, dual ceramic Belfast sinks with chrome mixer tap, breakfast counter with seating for two, (3) x glass display cabinets with downlighters and tempered glass shelving, (4) x ring chrome LED centre lights, light-grey subway tiling to splashback, undercounter downlighters, patterned ceramic floor throughout.\n\nConservatory: - 8.1m x 3.9m\nfull span from front to back, with featured vaulted ceiling, pendant centre lights, triple aspect windows, carpet floor covering, display area with tempered glass shelving, uPVC double clear glass doors.\n\nBedroom 1: - 3.6m x 2.5m\nwith high quality carpet floor covering, built-in storage each side of bed, centre light.Open Arch to:\n\nDressing Room 1: - 2.7m x 2.7m\nwith carpet floor covering, (3) x built-in wardrobes,\n\nBedroom 2: - 4.2m x 2.7m\nwith high quality carpet floor covering, centre light, window facing onto rear garden.\n\nDressing Room 2: - 3.2m x 1.7m\nwith carpet floor covering, built-in wall-to-wall wardrobes, centre light.\n\nBathroom: - 3.4m x 1.7m\nwith modern sanitary ware in white comprising of a dual flush w.c, vanity basin with tampered glass shelve and mirror over, bath with (2) x polished steel taps, vertical towel heater, patterned “Henley” ceramic tiled floor, light-grey subway tiling to walls, chrome centre light, coved area with tampered glass storage shelves.\n\nLanding: - 3.5m x 1.5m\nwith carpet floor covering, chrome inset lights.\n\nBedroom 3: - 5.1m x 4.4m\nwith high quality carpet floor covering, Velux window, chrome inset ceiling lights.\n\nEn-suite Bathroom: - 4.4m x 4.3m\nat widest point with modern sanitary ware in white comprising of a dual flush w.c, dual vanity basins with tempered glass shelve and mirror over, bath with chrome mixer taps, large shower cubicle with waterfall and adjustable shower heads, tampered glass screen, patterned “Henley” ceramic floor tiles, throughout,Velux window, light-grey subway tiling with walls, chrome inset ceiling lights.\n\nLaundry Room: - 2.6m x 2.5m\n“L-shaped” at widest point, built-in pullout storage cabinet, patterned “Henley” ceramic floor tiles, LED centre light.\n\nGarage / Store: - 6.3m x 3.7m\nwith power and lighting.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Instantly appealing three-bedroom detached residence extending to circa 148 sq.m / 1,593 sq.ft in area.</li><li> Upgraded and extended by the current owners in 2022/2023 to a very high standard throughout.</li><li> Peaceful rural setting positioned just under 3 kms from Carrick Village and it's essential local amenities.</li><li> Occupying a stunning and tranquil countryside setting with far-reaching views over the surrounding hills and rolling landscape.</li><li> Set on mature, landscaped gardens spanning c. 1.18 acres offering a high degree of privacy.</li><li> Gardens have been carefully nurtured to create a private oasis for wildlife, attracting guinea fowl, native birds, bees,</li><li> butterflies and other wildlife.</li><li> Bright, character-filled accommodation tastefully presented throughout.</li><li> uPVC double glazed windows throughout.</li><li> Oil fired centre heating external boiler and 3-zone EPH timeclock.</li><li> Three generous reception rooms.</li><li> Spacious snug/living room incorporating a formal dining area and oak staircase.</li><li> Well-appointed kitchen/diner with solid fitted units, chunky wooden worktops, Belfast sinks, integrated appliances, induction hob, double oven and breakfast counter.</li><li> Impressive full-span conservatory with vaulted ceiling, triple-aspect windows and direct access to the outside.</li><li> Three well-proportioned bedrooms, including a large first-floor bedroom with en-suite bathroom.</li><li> Separate laundry room, store and garage, all adding excellent practical storage and utility space.</li><li> Detached garage / store (c. 23.3 sqm) previously granted planning under reference no 2051257 for the conversion into a hobby / games room.</li><li> A unique countryside home combining upgraded accommodation, privacy, wildlife-friendly gardens and genuine lifestyle appeal.</li><li> As part of the extension works, the house was fully replumbed and rewired.</li><li> Viewings by prior arrangement with DNG Dorrian on 074 97 31291.</ul>"
      },
